INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (3, 'SEPTIC.TXT', 'Care and feeding of your septic system', 1277, 'SysOp', 1792371656037, 'approved', 1, '=====================================================================
  CARE AND FEEDING OF YOUR SEPTIC SYSTEM
  a public service text from The Septic Tankz BBS
=====================================================================

HOW IT WORKS
  Everything from the house flows into the tank and separates into
  three layers:

    SCUM ........ grease and light stuff that floats on top
    EFFLUENT .... the mostly-clear liquid in the middle
    SLUDGE ...... the heavy solids that sink to the bottom

  Only the middle layer leaves the tank, through the outlet tee, and
  soaks away into the leach field. Bacteria in the tank slowly break
  down the rest.

KEEP IT HAPPY
  * Have it pumped every 3 to 5 years, more often for a big family.
  * Spread out laundry. Ten loads on Saturday floods the leach field.
  * Fix running toilets. A trickle all day is a lot of water.
  * Don''t drive or park on the leach field.

NEVER FLUSH
  * Grease and cooking oil
  * "Flushable" wipes (they are not)
  * Paint, solvents, or medicines
  * Floppy disks (you know who you are)

SIGNS OF TROUBLE
  Slow drains, gurgling pipes, a soggy lawn over the leach field, or a
  smell outside. Call a pro before it calls you.

                                         -- ThE PLuMBeR, your SysOp
', 'text/plain');
INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (3, 'RATIOS.TXT', 'How ratios work on this board. READ THIS', 880, 'SysOp', 1792371656037, 'approved', 1, 'UPLOAD/DOWNLOAD RATIOS ON THE SEPTIC TANKZ
==========================================

This board runs on ratios, like every good board does. You earn
download credit by uploading.

THE MAIN BOARD
  * New users start with 2,048K of download credit.
  * Every byte you upload earns 5 bytes of credit (1:5).
  * Credit is added when the SysOp validates your upload, not before.
  * Files marked FREE cost nothing to download.
  * Reading text files on-line is always free.

UPLOADING
  * Upload from the file area you want the file to go in.
  * New uploads wait in the SysOp''s validation queue. Junk, viruses
    and anything we don''t want to host get flushed without credit.
  * Give your file a real description. "cool file" is not one.

YOUR STATS
  Check [Y] Your Stats on the main menu any time to see your
  uploads, downloads and remaining credit.

Leeches will be flushed.
', 'text/plain');
INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (3, 'NETIQUET.TXT', 'How not to be a lamer in the message bases', 648, 'SysOp', 1792371656037, 'approved', 1, 'HOW NOT TO BE A LAMER IN THE MESSAGE BASES
------------------------------------------

 1. Read before you post. Somebody already asked.
 2. Don''t type in ALL CAPS. We can hear you fine.
 3. Quote only what you''re replying to, not the whole message.
 4. Put something real in the subject line. "HELP!!!" is not a subject.
 5. Keep flame wars out of General. Take it to E-mail.
 6. Say thanks when someone helps you. It costs nothing.
 7. Don''t post the same message in every base.
 8. Upload something now and then. A board is only as good as its users.
 9. There is one phone line. Log off when you''re done.

Be excellent to each other. Party on.
', 'text/plain');
INSERT INTO files (area_id, filename, descr, size, uploader, uploaded_at, status, free, content, ctype) VALUES (3, 'MODEMFAQ.TXT', 'Modem FAQ: noises, init strings, call waiting', 798, 'SysOp', 1792371656037, 'approved', 1, 'MODEM FAQ (the short version)
-----------------------------

Q: What do all those noises mean when I connect?
A: The two modems are introducing themselves. First a 2100 Hz answer
   tone, then they probe the line and agree on the fastest speed it
   can handle. The hiss at the end is them training their equalizers.

Q: Why do I keep getting dropped?
A: Usually call waiting. Dial *70, before the number to turn it off
   for the call. Or somebody picked up the extension. MOM.

Q: What does ATZ do?
A: Resets the modem to its saved settings. ATDT dials with tones.
   ATH0 hangs up. +++ gets the modem''s attention mid-call.

Q: Zmodem, Ymodem or Xmodem?
A: Zmodem. It''s faster and it can resume a broken download.

Q: Why is the line always busy?
A: There''s one line. Try again in a few minutes.
', 'text/plain');
